{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":223251,"num_turns":1,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"65e58169-63c2-4824-bc68-ecd71d4d6e3d","total_cost_usd":1.1160825,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":65401,"cache_read_input_tokens":16967,"output_tokens":16296,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":65401,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":16296,"cache_read_input_tokens":16967,"cache_creation_input_tokens":65401,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":65401},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":46104,"outputTokens":15,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.046179,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-opus-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":16296,"cacheReadInputTokens":16967,"cacheCreationInputTokens":65401,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.0699035000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\n  \"agent\": \"playtester\",\n  \"verdict\": \"targets_missed\",\n  \"summary\": \"Flown, this config never reaches orbit at base fuel and never rewards a second braking pass — a single committed entry is the cheapest descent in all nine band/load cases — and the grid shows why: skim cooling and unstaged survivability sit on opposite ends of the ballistic coefficient, so no world in 2916 satisfies both.\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"no_band_reachable_at_base_config\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.6\",\n      \"claim\": \"game_params balance_notes assert the base ship reaches the suborbital band with ~180 m/s of margin (1525 m/s available against ~1300 m/s of ascent), making fuel_tank tier 1 the first real purchase rather than a prerequisite for flying at all.\",\n      \"measured\": \"All three ascents report reached=false, 'out of fuel before circularising': suborbital stops with 290.17 kg (24.2%) unspent, low with 210.80 kg (17.6%), high with 153.37 kg (12.8%). Not one band in the shipping slice is attainable at fuel_capacity_kg 1200. The grid satisfies bands_reachable in 43.8% of configurations and fuel_margin_sane in 18.9%, so reachable ascents plainly exist in the space.\",\n      \"severity\": \"blocking\",\n      \"kind\": \"tuning\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ablation_optimum_is_always_one_pass\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.1\",\n      \"claim\": \"The GDD requires the cheapest descent to be 2-4 committed passes, 'never a single plunge and never feathering', and game_params.ablation.cost_curve asserts minima at index 0 / 1 / 2 for suborbital / low / high with margins of 0.52 / 1.10 / 0.55 plate-percent.\",\n      \"measured\": \"cheapest_pass_count is 1 in every one of the nine band x load descents, and ablation_pct rises monotonically with pass count in every series without exception: suborbital full hold 18.5 -> 22.4 -> 24.3 -> 25.9%; low full hold 15.8 -> 21.6 -> 23.8 -> 25.5%; high full hold 16.3 -> 23.2 -> 25.4 -> 26.8%. The second pass costs 3.9 / 5.8 / 6.9 plate-percent and buys nothing back. The asserted low-band and high-band minima at indices 1 and 2 do not appear at any load. This is §4.5 risk 1 landing: with measured cooling, no setting of cycle_toll_base_pct or cycle_toll_growth produces a U-curve, because the toll would have to fall below ~0.2%/cycle with zero growth, which is the anti-feathering mechanism removed.\",\n      \"severity\": \"blocking\",\n      \"kind\": \"design\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"skim_cooling_three_times_weaker_than_priced\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.1\",\n      \"claim\": \"ablation.skim_heat_multiplier is [1.0, 0.92, 0.87, 0.86] — an 8% cut in entry heat for the first skim, 13% for two — and the balance_notes concede it is 'a considered guess, not a measurement', asking the Playtester to adopt the measured array and re-price.\",\n      \"measured\": \"Measured at the deepest commit: suborbital [1, 0.951, 0.897, 0.684], low [1, 0.977, 0.955, 0.934], high [1, 0.984, 0.968, 0.954]. The first skim from the high band removes 1.6% of entry heat, not 8% — a factor of 5 short, and the bands that most need cooling cool least. Each skim still charges a flat 1.28 plate-percent of skim heat plus its cycle toll, so it is priced at roughly five times what it delivers. The suborbital 3-skim figure of 0.684 is not comparable: that run reports commit_dv_ms 0, i.e. the skims deorbited the ship outright rather than preceding a commit.\",\n      \"severity\": \"blocking\",\n      \"kind\": \"design\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"no_world_satisfies_every_target\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"4.5\",\n      \"claim\": \"The design assumes its seven measurable targets are jointly achievable once the numbers are right — that aerobraking, survivable unstaged braking passes, and a rising difficulty curve can all coexist in one world.\",\n      \"measured\": \"Across 2916 configurations best_score is 7 of 8; nothing scores 8. The conflict traces to ballistic coefficient and is visible in the top list: the 60 km worlds get real skim cooling (multipliers [1, 0.798, 0.82, 0.82]) at beta 44.4-133.3 but their unstaged pass peaks at 413-414 heat, four times the plate; the 160 km worlds survive unstaged (peak 28-69) at beta 400-1333 but their skims do nothing (multipliers [1, 0.996, 0.993, 0.990]). Satisfaction rates confirm the squeeze: unstaged_pass_survivable 13.9%, fuel_margin_sane 18.9%, difficulty_rises_with_band 31.8%, bands_reachable 43.8%, skimming_cools_the_entry 44.1%. The shipped world sits at staged beta 171.4, between the two poles, and gets a weak version of both.\",\n      \"severity\": \"significant\",\n      \"kind\": \"design\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"difficulty_falls_with_band_on_the_optimised_descent\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.7\",\n      \"claim\": \"§2.3.7: 'Reentry speed - and therefore heat - scales with the altitude you return from, so the value curve and the risk curve rise together.' game_params.heat_index encodes that as 83 / 100 / 119.\",\n      \"measured\": \"Two answers, depending on how the entry is flown, and they point opposite ways. At the deepest commit the curve is steeper than claimed: peak heat 100 / 131.5 / 163.1 (ratios 1.00 / 1.32 / 1.63 against the params' 1.00 / 1.20 / 1.43). But at the pass-count-optimised commit the curve inverts — full-hold cheapest ablation is 18.5% from suborbital, 15.8% from low and 16.3% from high, with peak heat 95 / 90 / 91, and empty is 7.0 / 6.1 / 6.2%. The return leg from the top of the sky is the cheapest one available, which is the failure §4.5 risk 2 is written against. Only 31.8% of the grid satisfies difficulty_rises_with_band, so the target is fragile wherever it is placed.\",\n      \"severity\": \"significant\",\n      \"kind\": \"design\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"unstaged_pass_measured_at_the_wrong_mass\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.1\",\n      \"claim\": \"baseline notes quote the unstaged ballistic coefficient as 1959 kg/m2 (2400 kg fuelled stack over Cd 0.35 x A 3.5), and unstaged_heat_multiplier 3.5 is tuned to keep a shallow unstaged braking pass survivable while making a committed unstaged entry fatal.\",\n      \"measured\": \"The sweep reports unstaged_kg_m2 = 734.7, which is exactly 900 / (0.35 x 3.5) — the dry mass, not the fuelled stack. The unstaged passes it then clears (suborbital peak 73, low peak 83, both survivable against the 100 cargo-damage line) were flown 2.7x too light. A slipperier 1959 kg/m2 stack decelerates less per pass and penetrates deeper, so the real margin is narrower than 73 and 83 suggest. Given the grid satisfies unstaged_pass_survivable in only 13.9% of configurations, this margin is the one least able to absorb being wrong.\",\n      \"severity\": \"significant\",\n      \"kind\": \"tuning\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"descent_wall_clock_confirms_time_warp_is_mandatory\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"4.1\",\n      \"claim\": \"§4.1 defers time compression, 'mitigated by scoping the planet small enough that a two-band orbit period is under a minute'. The Researcher and the balance_notes both record that this mitigation failed and that warp must ship.\",\n      \"measured\": \"Simulated descent duration: 1.06 h for a direct suborbital entry, 1.91 h for a single-skim low-band descent, 3.42 h for three skims from low, 4.16 h for three skims from high, 4.31 h at the shallowest high-band commit. The cheapest descents measured here are single-pass, which is also the shortest — so as currently tuned the game rewards the player for skipping the mechanic that costs the hours. Any fix that restores multi-pass descents restores the multi-hour descent with it.\",\n      \"severity\": \"significant\",\n      \"kind\": \"design\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"full_hold_descent_speed_is_asserted_not_measured\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.2\",\n      \"claim\": \"landing.descent_speed_full_hold_ms 4.7 puts a full hold inside the 5 m/s soft-landing line, with the balance_notes deriving an implied 603.6 m2 canopy at parachute_drag_coefficient 1.8.\",\n      \"measured\": \"Touchdown is 4.70 m/s full hold, 4.07 m/s half, 3.32 m/s empty in every single descent case, and soft_landing is true throughout — but the sweep's own inferred[] block states landing.parachute_area_m2 is absent from the params and was solved backwards from the 4.7 m/s claim. The agreement is arithmetic, not evidence. The sqrt(mass) scaling it implies is real and does hold across loads (4.70 / 4.07 / 3.32 tracks sqrt(1800/1350/900) to within 0.01 m/s), so the Storage-vs-Parachute pairing stands; the absolute number does not, until the area is a field.\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"kind\": \"tuning\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"greed_penalty_and_anti_feathering_both_hold\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.5\",\n      \"claim\": \"§2.3.5 and §4.5 risk 2: cargo mass must make the ride home measurably harder, and §2.3.1 requires that feathering never be the cheap path.\",\n      \"measured\": \"Both confirmed at fixed gear tier. Empty to full hold raises cheapest ablation from 7.0 to 18.5% (suborbital), 6.1 to 15.8% (low), 6.2 to 16.3% (high) — a 2.6x plate bill for a doubled mass — and peak heat from 65 to 95, 62 to 90, 62 to 91. Feathering is priced out decisively: 16 passes from the low band empty costs 29.4% against 6.1% for one, and 25 passes from the high band full costs 56.8% against 16.3%. The grid agrees this is the easy half — greed_costs_something 84.3%, skim_benefit_saturates 87.7%. Half of §2.3.1's requirement is met; it is the 'never a single plunge' half that is not.\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"kind\": \"tuning\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"proposed_changes\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"flight.fuel_capacity_kg\",\n      \"current\": 1200,\n      \"proposed\": 1800,\n      \"reason\": \"Raises the base delta-v from 2200*ln(2400/1200) = 1525 m/s to 2200*ln(3000/1200) = 2016 m/s so the suborbital band is reachable at all before any purchase; it costs launch TWR (22000/(3000*4.0) = 1.83, down from 2.29), makes the unstaged stack heavier still on coarse braking passes, and forces the fuel_tank tier 1 and 2 values to be rebased above it.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"ablation.skim_heat_multiplier\",\n      \"current\": [1, 0.92, 0.87, 0.86],\n      \"proposed\": [1, 0.977, 0.955, 0.934],\n      \"reason\": \"Replaces the balance_notes' acknowledged guess with the low-band measurement, which the notes themselves asked for; it costs the entire ablation optimum story, because once the real cooling is priced no toll setting makes a second pass pay, and cost_curve and optimal_skims must be recomputed from it rather than kept.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"ablation.cycle_toll_growth\",\n      \"current\": 1.25,\n      \"proposed\": 1,\n      \"reason\": \"Adopts §4.5 risk 1's own named fallback — flat per-pass cost plus a hard cap — instead of hunting a U-curve the sweep shows does not exist; it costs the escalating-toll elegance, and on its own it does not restore a 2-4 pass optimum, so it must ship with the cap below and with multi-pass made a survivability requirement rather than an economy.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"ablation.max_passes\",\n      \"current\": null,\n      \"proposed\": 4,\n      \"reason\": \"The cap half of the §4.5 fallback, replacing the growth term as the anti-feathering device now that growth is flat; it costs a new field the Coder must honour, and it forecloses the 16-25 pass descents the sweep found reachable (29.4% and 56.8% plate) rather than merely pricing them out.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"ablation.optimal_skims\",\n      \"current\": {\"suborbital\": 0, \"low\": 1, \"high\": 2},\n      \"proposed\": {\"suborbital\": 0, \"low\": 0, \"high\": 0},\n      \"reason\": \"Stops the params asserting an optimum the simulator finds nowhere — cheapest_pass_count is 1 in all nine cases; it costs the design its claimed skim gradient, and it should be read as a flag that the rule needs changing from 'multi-pass is cheapest' to 'multi-pass is required to survive the upper bands', which is the version heat_capacity can actually enforce.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"ablation.heat_index\",\n      \"current\": {\"suborbital\": 83, \"low\": 100, \"high\": 119},\n      \"proposed\": {\"suborbital\": 100, \"low\": 131, \"high\": 163},\n      \"reason\": \"Uses the measured deepest-commit peaks (100 / 131.5 / 163.1) instead of the v^3 estimate, which understated the band spread by a third; it costs the band-gate arithmetic in the balance_notes, because at heat_capacity 100 a direct low-band entry now exceeds the cargo-damage line by 31 and a high-band one by 63, so heat_capacity and the heat_shield tier values must be re-gated against these before anyone flies it.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"landing.parachute_area_m2\",\n      \"current\": null,\n      \"proposed\": 603.6,\n      \"reason\": \"Makes explicit the canopy area the sweep had to solve for out of descent_speed_full_hold_ms, so touchdown speed becomes a measurement rather than a restatement of the claim; it costs nothing except admitting the current 4.70 m/s agreement is circular.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"baseline.planet.surface_gravity_ms2\",\n      \"current\": 4,\n      \"proposed\": 3,\n      \"reason\": \"Last resort if the fuel raise is judged too blunt: every top-scoring grid configuration uses g = 3.0, and it cuts suborbital circular speed from 730 to 632 m/s (about 13% off the ascent budget) and lowers every terminal velocity with it; it costs a full re-derivation of the Researcher's baseline — orbital speeds, periods, ballistic coefficients and the parachute area all move — so it is a bigger change than the ascent problem alone justifies.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"confidence_notes\": [\n    \"The two sweep blocks disagree about the same descents and I have treated them as different commit depths rather than as an error, but I cannot verify that. The heat_scale_calibration says an empty single-pass suborbital descent is normalised to 100, while the descents block reports peak_heat 65 for exactly that flight and the skims block reports 100 at entry_depth_m 0. My reading is that entry_depth_m 0 is the deepest commit and the descents block chooses a shallower optimised one (braking_altitude_m 47711 for that case) — which is also why the band ordering inverts between the blocks. If that reading is wrong, the difficulty_falls_with_band finding is the first thing to fall over.\",\n    \"The ascent block reports 'out of fuel before circularising' while simultaneously reporting 290.17 kg (24.2%) of fuel remaining, which cannot both be literally true. I trust the direction of that result (no band reached at 1200 kg) more than the magnitude, and the 1800 kg proposal is sized from the params' own rocket-equation budget rather than from the sweep's margin figures. Someone should establish what the ascent model's failure criterion actually is before that number is committed.\",\n    \"The unstaged braking result is measured at 900 kg (beta 734.7) when the configuration it represents carries a fuelled stage at 2400 kg (beta 1959). Both unstaged survivability figures — suborbital 73, low 83 — are therefore optimistic by an unknown amount, and unstaged_pass_survivable is the scarcest target in the grid at 13.9%. Re-run that case at the fuelled mass before trusting unstaged_heat_multiplier 3.5.\",\n    \"The grid worlds are not this world. The configurations that get real skim cooling are 60 km-radius bodies at g = 3.0 with a 16.8 km atmosphere — a different game with different orbital periods, not a tuning of the shipped planet. I have used the satisfaction rates to bound what is achievable in principle and to separate tuning from design, which is what they support; I have not treated any top config as a drop-in candidate.\",\n    \"None of §2.3.4 was flown. Tether shear, hold force, latch and swing jerk, tether-count-versus-EVA-fuel and the two catalog_concerns the economy agent raised all rest on algebra in the balance_notes and on nothing in this sweep. The steady-tow no-shear identity is sound as algebra; the impulsive coefficients (latch_jerk_coefficient 0.6, swing_jerk_coefficient 2.5) are entirely unmeasured, and §4.5 risk 3 remains exactly as open as it was before this run.\",\n    \"The simulator is a point mass with a perfect pilot. off_retrograde_penalty is never exercised because attitude error does not exist; the plasma-to-chute window, the chute-shred rule, hull glow and every part of pillar three are unmodelled. Every soft_landing=true in this sweep means 'the physics permits it', not 'a player achieves it'. The anxiety check in §3.3 Checkpoint 3 is untouched by anything I can measure, and the single-pass-is-cheapest result would probably feel worse than it reads: the descent it rewards is the one with no decision in it.\"\n  ]\n}","ttft_ms":136308,"ttft_stream_ms":1792,"time_to_request_ms":196,"type":"result","duration_ms":215072,"uuid":"447f3327-1ad8-4cbf-a908-7bee0ad5de8a"}
